     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe, and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single oral dose is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum daily prescription dose is **3200 mg/day** (800 mg four times daily).\n- This order is 2\u00d7 the single-dose maximum and 2\u00d7 the daily maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). Total daily dose is often mixed up with the per-dose amount.\n2. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum prescription dose)\n3. **Something else.** For example, if this was meant as a single 1600 mg dose, or there's a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, tell me the reason. I can then decide how to proceed and record it in an order note.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
